this morning clark county started the  long process to build a formal memorial  to those affected  by the one october tragedy committee  members involved in this say it could  take several  years for the project to actually be  built and right now the committee is  simply seeking public input  the hope is to honor victims and  survivors while also highlighting how  the community came together on las vegas  darkest night  since the process just started questions  on funding and a location  are still a long way from being answered  i think it's going to be a very  emotional journey  but in that is a healing journey  we want to make sure that we do it right  we don't want to rush it but we also  want to be respectful of time  this of course is going to be separate  from the healing garden downtown  60 people were killed in the one october  attack three years ago however today  a group of survivors and family of  victims  asked this new committee to keep the  death toll at 58.  they believe that that number represents  the 58 people who did not get to return  home  on one october
 

